[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-09c3cbac-e2e5-4d78-89b0-9f1bf9e1b000\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p><strong>Wed 19 Nov 2025 14:10 - 14:20 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/ase-2025/ase-2025-venue-grand-hall-4\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Grand Hall 4</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/ase-2025/ase-2025-papers#program\" class=\"navigate\">Program Analysis 2</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/raffikhatchadourian\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Raffi Khatchadourian</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"09c3cbac-e2e5-4d78-89b0-9f1bf9e1b000\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Spinner: Detecting Locking Violations in the eBPF Runtime</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>The eBPF technology is widely used for many applications including tracing, packet filtering, network usage monitoring, and so on. The versatility of eBPF allows the kernel\u2019s capabilities to be extended without needing to modify source code or load kernel modules. However, the eBPF subsystem may introduce new bugs that could lead to crashes, data loss, and other issues that can negatively impact system stability, reliability, availability, security, and overall performance. Specifically, locking violations, which occur when locks are not used correctly, can lead to problems like deadlocks and system hangs. Since eBPF operates at the kernel level, errors here have far-reaching consequences.</p>\n<p>To tackle this issue, we present Gopher, a tool for detecting locking violations in the eBPF runtime. Gopher uses static analysis to (1) detect cases of context confusion where incorrect locking primitives are used in eBPF helper functions given their execution context, and (2) identify locks in helper functions that can be called recursively using nested eBPF programs. Both of these situations could result in deadlocks. So far, Gopher has identified 34 locking violation bugs in the eBPF subsystem in Linux, only 5 of which were previously found by Syzbot.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/priyagovindasamy\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Priya Govindasamy<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California, Irvine</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/josephbursey\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Joseph Bursey<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California, Irvine</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/hsinweihung1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Hsin-Wei Hung<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Meta</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/ardalansani\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Ardalan Amiri <span class=\"name-visual-sep\"></span>Sani<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California, Irvine</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2025/ase-2025-papers/202/Spinner-Detecting-Locking-Violations-in-the-eBPF-Runtime\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-09c3cbac-e2e5-4d78-89b0-9f1bf9e1b000').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
